      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Changing locations in game Ugh, definately would avoid that if possible. \n\nIf VRChat could find or buy a widget for that, sure, but otherwise it might be way too much hassle. I just feel that navigating drives and folders in VR is a horrible idea in designing a UI (user interface) for and also using it.\n\nIf you can get over using notepad and maybe an online JSON lint (I haven't actually looked at a config file in a year is my excuse if it's not JSON) \n\nBut yeah, if you can stomach editing a config file, you can make changes today. I guess also have to learn about file extensions, thanks to windows hiding them by default. \n\nI do see merit in separating the world and avatar cache, but yeah, better off being done in the config file. What I would ask for of I was writing the feature request would be an optional separate world cache, then people could specify a pile of storage elsewhere for worlds.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
